  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116386",
      "title": "What Is Routing?",
      "lectureOrder": 267,
      "videoOrder": 255,
      "sourceHash": "1fcb02266914c2f9aaf5184ffe64d836e9453bda8272940a8c674f771c9109fa",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 3.69,
          "en": "So what exactly is routing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.69,
          "end": 6.36,
          "en": "What does this term mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.36,
          "end": 10.59,
          "en": "Well, Angular applications are typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.59,
          "end": 15.36,
          "en": "single page applications, which in the end simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.36,
          "end": 18.51,
          "en": "that there's only a single HTML page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.51,
          "end": 20.49,
          "en": "that's being served by the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.49,
          "end": 24.69,
          "en": "that's hosting your Angular application to the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.69,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "so to the user visiting the website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 30.12,
          "en": "that's requesting this website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.12,
          "end": 33.12,
          "en": "so this Angular application therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.12,
          "end": 36.42,
          "en": "There's only a single HTML page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.42,
          "end": 39.18,
          "en": "But of course, since we're using Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.18,
          "end": 42.18,
          "en": "to build a feature rich web application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.18,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "that single page often gives us a web application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 51.03,
          "en": "a website that feels like it consists of multiple pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.03,
          "end": 54.27,
          "en": "And indeed, you often might want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.27,
          "end": 57.75,
          "en": "to have multiple pages kind of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.75,
          "end": 60.39,
          "en": "You want that one single HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.39,
          "end": 62.85,
          "en": "that loads the Angular application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 66,
          "en": "But then once the application is up and running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66,
          "end": 68.82,
          "en": "in the browser of your website visitor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.82,
          "end": 71.49,
          "en": "then you might wanna give that visitor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.49,
          "end": 75.24,
          "en": "the illusion of switching between different pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.24,
          "end": 79.05,
          "en": "For example, in that app we did build earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.05,
          "end": 83.25,
          "en": "where we could select a user to see the tasks of that user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.25,
          "end": 86.76,
          "en": "and where we could then start adding a new task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.76,
          "end": 90.75,
          "en": "If you think about it, these different screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.75,
          "end": 94.74000000000001,
          "en": "which we loaded as we navigated through the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.74000000000001,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "in the end, could be considered different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 99.21000000000001,
          "en": "that are being loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.21000000000001,
          "end": 102.09,
          "en": "because we see quite some different content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.09,
          "end": 104.91,
          "en": "on the page as the UI changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.91,
          "end": 107.67,
          "en": "And that's what the term routing means.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.67,
          "end": 111.15,
          "en": "It simply means that you wanna update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.15,
          "end": 114.6,
          "en": "as the user navigates through your webpage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.6,
          "end": 118.77000000000001,
          "en": "You typically also wanna update the browser address bar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 121.86,
          "en": "so that links to different parts of your website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.86,
          "end": 123.57,
          "en": "can be shared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.57,
          "end": 127.83,
          "en": "And as it turns out, Angular supports this behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.83,
          "end": 132.72,
          "en": "and Angular allows you to implement client-side routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.72,
          "end": 134.88,
          "en": "so that the Angular framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.88,
          "end": 139.17000000000002,
          "en": "takes care of updating the URL, reading the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.17000000000002,
          "end": 141.66,
          "en": "and of loading different components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.66,
          "end": 145.05,
          "en": "depending on the currently active URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 147.57,
          "en": "That's what the term routing means,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.57,
          "end": 150.27,
          "en": "and that's a feature baked into Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.27,
          "end": 153.09300000000002,
          "en": "which we'll now explore in greater detail.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
